source "Kconfig.zephyr"

config SAMPLE_IPC_INFER_LIVE_I2S
	bool "Capture live from the I2S receiver through a pipeline"
	help
	  Build the host side as an mpipe pipeline that captures from I2S and
	  tees the audio two ways: to the codec so it can be heard, and to the
	  peer core for inference. Without this the host sends baked-in clips,
	  which is what lets the sample check the answers it gets back.

config SAMPLE_IPC_INFER_RATE
	int "Capture sample rate (Hz)"
	default 16000
	depends on SAMPLE_IPC_INFER_LIVE_I2S
	help
	  Pinned rather than negotiated. micro_speech is trained at 16 kHz, and
	  the peer sized its ring periods to match; a negotiation that landed
	  elsewhere would satisfy every element and still be the wrong audio.

config SAMPLE_IPC_INFER_GAIN_PERCENT
	int "Gain applied on the audible branch (percent)"
	default 300
	range 0 1000
	depends on SAMPLE_IPC_INFER_LIVE_I2S
	help
	  Applied only to the branch that reaches the codec, so monitoring can
	  be made loud enough to hear without changing what the model receives.
